				\begin{document}$${\theta }_{ij}={t}_{\max }\sigma$$\end{document}θij=tmaxσ

In the step (3) of the proposed method, the 3D spherical embedding method proposed by Wilson et al.27 is used to estimate the intersection points of the normal vectors, using the dihedral angles θij computed in step (2) as initial distance values. The goal of the 3D spherical embedding is to find an embedding of the intersection points with Euler angles (αi, βi), i = (1, 2, …, n), on the 3D unit spherical surface, such that the distortion of the distances, ε, defined as follows is minimized:5\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
