To estimate the initial value of the angles between local X-axis vectors in step (4), the common line information as well as the dihedral angles after the spherical embedding are used. As shown in Fig. 9, for any two images i and j, a coordinate system can be setup such that image i is on the XY plane, and the common line between the two images is along the X-axis. If Cij represents the angle between the common line and the local X-axis vector of the image i, Cji represents the angle between the common line and the local X-axis vector of the image j, \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
